From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: B Honey <9922368+Mhsbrian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:31:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 23/23] nvk: optionally report the NVIDIA kernel driver's
 version as driverVersion

With VK_VENDOR_ID 0x10de, apps and layers decode driverVersion the way
NVIDIA's driver encodes it (10.8.8.6 bits). Mesa's 26.2.5 then reads as
NVIDIA driver 26.0.128.5, and ANGLE applies every workaround for NVIDIA
drivers older than 421 to 535: no graphics pipeline libraries, no SPIR-V
1.4, a wait for submissions before query results, an externally
synchronized pipeline cache, a point-size clamp.

NVK_NVIDIA_DRIVER_VERSION=MAJOR.MINOR[.PATCH] (on Android also
debug.mesa.nvk.nvidia.driver.version) reports that version in NVIDIA's
encoding instead, e.g. the kernel driver's 615.78.08. Off by default; for
the A/B of ANGLE's NVIDIA conditions on the G14 (Ruby's ANGLE ignores
its own debug.angle.feature_overrides_* for Vulkan features).

ANAL-311 (GoodBook).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c
index 1a5b9a4..2547564 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c
@@ -850,9 +850,26 @@ nvk_get_device_properties(const struct nvk_instance *instance,
       supported_shader_stages |=
          VK_SHADER_STAGE_TASK_BIT_EXT | VK_SHADER_STAGE_MESH_BIT_EXT;
 
+   /* VK_VENDOR_ID 0x10de makes apps and layers read driverVersion the way
+    * NVIDIA encodes it (10.8.8.6 bits), so Mesa's 26.2.5 reads as NVIDIA
+    * driver 26.0.128.5 and ANGLE applies every workaround for NVIDIA drivers
+    * older than 421 to 535 (no graphics pipeline libraries, no SPIR-V 1.4,
+    * waits for query results).  NVK_NVIDIA_DRIVER_VERSION=MAJOR.MINOR[.PATCH]
+    * (on Android also debug.mesa.nvk.nvidia.driver.version) reports that
+    * version in NVIDIA's encoding instead, e.g. the kernel driver's 615.78.08.
+    */
+   uint32_t driver_version = vk_get_driver_version();
+   const char *nvidia_version = os_get_option("NVK_NVIDIA_DRIVER_VERSION");
+   unsigned nv_major, nv_minor, nv_patch = 0;
+   if (nvidia_version != NULL &&
+       sscanf(nvidia_version, "%u.%u.%u", &nv_major, &nv_minor,
+              &nv_patch) >= 2 &&
+       nv_major < 1024 && nv_minor < 256 && nv_patch < 256)
+      driver_version = (nv_major << 22) | (nv_minor << 14) | (nv_patch << 6);
+
    *properties = (struct vk_properties) {
       .apiVersion = nvk_get_vk_version(info),
-      .driverVersion = vk_get_driver_version(),
+      .driverVersion = driver_version,
       .vendorID = instance->drirc.debug.force_vk_vendor != 0 ?
                   instance->drirc.debug.force_vk_vendor : NVIDIA_VENDOR_ID,
       .deviceID = info->device_id,
